This useEffect lacks a mechanism to prevent tracking errors after component unmounts. If the component unmounts while errors are present, the effect could still execute or cause issues during the unmount phase.

**Suggested fix**: Add proper cleanup or early return on unmount to prevent potential memory leaks:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
    if (isEmptyObject(errors)) {
        return;
    }

    // Track immediately and skip if component unmounts
    let isMounted = true;

    if (isMounted) {
        // ... error tracking logic
    }

    return () => {
        isMounted = false;
    };
}, [errors, ...]);
```

