**Issue**: If `player.play()` throws an error or fails immediately (before playback status updates), the subscription and player resources are never cleaned up, causing a memory leak.

**Impact**: Repeated failures to play sounds will accumulate player instances and subscriptions, leading to memory leaks.

**Suggested Fix**:
```tsx
const player = createAudioPlayer(source);

// Listen for playback completion to release resources
const subscription = player.addListener('playbackStatusUpdate', (status) => {
    if (!status.didJustFinish) {
        return;
    }

    subscription.remove();
    player.remove();
});

player.play().catch((error) => {
    // Clean up resources on play failure
    subscription.remove();
    player.remove();
    Log.alert('[Sound] Failed to play sound:', {message: error.message});
});
```

