This useEffect runs on **every render** because it has no dependency array. This causes the `querySelectorAll` DOM query and the `forEach` loop to execute unnecessarily on every render, creating a significant performance overhead.

Additionally, this creates a potential memory leak: if the component re-renders frequently (which is common in draggable lists), the effect will repeatedly query and modify DOM elements without proper cleanup.

**Suggested fix:**
Add a dependency array with `[children]` or use a ref callback pattern:

```tsx
// Option 1: Add dependency array
useEffect(() => {
    if (contentRef.current) {
        const focusableElements = contentRef.current.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(
            '[tabindex="0"], [role="button"], [role="menuitem"], button:not([tabindex="-1"]), a:not([tabindex="-1"])'
        );
        focusableElements.forEach((el) => {
            el.tabIndex = -1;
        });
    }
}, [children]);

// Option 2: Use ref callback (more efficient)
const contentRef = useCallback((node: HTMLDivElement | null) => {
    if (node) {
        const focusableElements = node.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(
            '[tabindex="0"], [role="button"], [role="menuitem"], button:not([tabindex="-1"]), a:not([tabindex="-1"])'
        );
        focusableElements.forEach((el) => {
            el.tabIndex = -1;
        });
    }
}, []);
```

